// The mounted Amulet of Glory, on a quest hall wall.
//
// This is NOT in poh_tablets.rs2, where it first went: that file is generated by tools/gentablets.py
// and the next run deleted it. Battery check 43 - "re-running the generator changes nothing" - is
// what caught it, which is the second time this round's worth of work has been saved by that check.
//
// OSRS lets you rub it for the same four destinations an Amulet of Glory gives, without charges, and
// those four were already written in general/scripts/enchanted_jewellry/amulet_of_glory.rs2.
//
// THAT CODE USED TO BE A LABEL THAT ATE A CHARGE off whatever was in last_slot. Called from a loc
// trigger, last_slot is whatever the player happens to be holding, so it would have quietly
// rewritten an inventory slot. The choice and the teleport are ~glory_teleport now and the label
// eats the charge itself.
//
// Only the amulet trophy carries op1=Rub - the Anti-Dragon Breath Shield and the Cape of Legends
// beside it have no op1 at all, and a trigger on an op a loc does not carry never fires - so this is
// one trigger rather than a family's worth, which is also why it is not in the generated file.
//
// The instance is freed on the way out: a teleport out of the house is still a way out of the house,
// and an instance nobody is standing in holds a slot until logout.

[oploc1,poh_trophy_amuletofglory_4]
~poh_glory_rub;

[proc,poh_glory_rub]
if (%poh_instance = null | instance_find(loc_coord) ! %poh_instance) {
    mes("You can only use that in your own house.");
    return;
}
if (~glory_teleport("The amulet's magic carries you away.") = false) {
    return;
}
~poh_free;
